{
  "id": "mercedes-egs5x-7226",
  "name": "Mercedes 722.6 5-speed automatic (NAG1) - EGS / EGS51 TCU",
  "kind": "tcu",
  "maker": "Siemens",
  "family": "722.6 EGS51",
  "vehicles": [
    "Mercedes W210 E-Class (1996-2002, pre-2000 TCU)",
    "W202 C-Class",
    "other pre-2000 722.6 applications with an EGS / EGS51 TCU"
  ],
  "validation": "synthetic-tested",
  "notes": "External (body-mounted) TCU of the 722.6 five-speed automatic. One CAN generation is defined: 'egs51' (pre-2000 EGS/EGS51 cars, 500 kbit/s), transcribed from the Ultimate-NAG52 project's hand-made EGS51 matrix. The frame layout of the later EGS52 (CAN-C, 2000+) cars is deliberately NOT included: it will be re-derived from a listen-only capture of the owner's own car. A W210 can be either generation; docs/MERCEDES-722.6.md describes how to tell them apart from a capture (by CAN ids, and by the gear coding in 0x218, which on EGS51 is R = 6 / P = 8). Everything here is passive CAN decode plus documentation: OpenTune does not transmit to this TCU, read its flash or know its checksum. Diagnostics: pre-2000 units are diagnosed on the K-line (C1 pin 1, see the database unit) with a protocol the cited sources do not document, so no diagnostic channel is declared. Tables describe the calibration structure of the open Ultimate-NAG52 replacement firmware (shift schedules, shift time, fill, TCC and adaptation maps), not the stock EGS flash layout, which is not publicly documented; no values are shipped. Validation: synthetic CAN frames built from the published layout only - nothing has been checked against a capture from a real car yet.",
